--
User-reported: `offsetof(CMD, in_dtype)` on an alias of a typedef'd
anonymous packed struct -- "offset-of of member failed to find
component".  In fact offsetof failed for EVERY C++ class: the C++ front
end qualifies component names (`S::d`) and keeps the spelling as the
base name, while the shared offsetof implementation looked the
designator up by component name.  N5008 [support.types.layout]/1:
offsetof(type, member-designator) has the same semantics as in C.
